<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad III of Granada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1257–<a href="/years/1314">1314</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad III was the third Nasrid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, reigning from 1302 to 1309. A patron of building, he constructed the main mosque of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alhambra">Alhambra</a>. His capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> in 1306 helped provoke an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, Aragon and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> against Granada, and in 1309 a palace revolt deposed him in favour of his brother Nasr; he died in confinement in 1314.</p></div>
